cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite the associated article. The associated manuscript is currently in submission; a permanent DOI will be added here after acceptance.
type: software
title: "PIS-CMOO — cross-site uncertainty-aware prediction, verification, and multi-objective decision-support framework for underground grouting"
version: 0.1.0-paper
date-released: 2026-09-20
repository-code: https://github.com/ailiwood/PIS-CMOO
license: see-LICENSE_PENDING.md
keywords:
  - underground grouting
  - leave-one-mine-out
  - TabDPT
  - CatBoost
  - conformal prediction
  - SHAP
  - NSGA-III
  - multi-objective optimization
  - cross-model verification
  - abstention
abstract: >-
  PIS-CMOO is a research codebase supporting a cross-site, uncertainty-aware
  decision-support framework for underground grouting. The framework combines
  leave-one-mine-out prediction (TabDPT primary, CatBoost optimization-response),
  one-sided conformal upper-bound calibration from mine-balanced cross-site
  residuals, SHAP interpretation, engineering-bound-aware NSGA-III multi-objective
  optimization, independent cross-model verification with abstention, and a single
  untouched external mine for honest evaluation. This public release ships the
  frozen pipeline scripts, frozen aggregate artifacts, a verification script that
  re-checks the manuscript's headline metrics, and a synthetic example dataset
  for software smoke testing. The real field dataset is not distributed due to
  commercial confidentiality.
